The root of the upstream archive contains a file named `VERSION`. Bazel passes
the repository root to dependents as a quote-include directory, and since MSVC
has no `-iquote`, it is passed as a regular `/I` include directory there. On the
case-insensitive Windows file system, `#include <version>` then resolves to this
file instead of the C++ standard header, which breaks any dependent that pulls
in `<version>`, directly or through headers such as `<bitset>`.

The file is not used by the build, so it is removed.

diff --git a/VERSION b/VERSION
deleted file mode 100644
index b52282a..0000000
--- a/VERSION
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1 +0,0 @@
-2.10.4
